---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SOCIAL } from '../config/site';
import '../styles/article.css';

const updated = '13 August 2026';
---
<Base title="Terms & Conditions · Team StormBreaker" description="The terms for using the Team StormBreaker website and the open-source software we publish.">
  <main>
    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <article class="article">
          <a class="back" href="/">← Back home</a>
          <header class="article-head">
            <div class="nc-meta"><span class="nc-tag">Legal</span><span class="nc-sep">/</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
            <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
          </header>

          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              By using <strong>stormbreaker.squadri.me</strong> and the software we publish, you agree to
              these terms. Team StormBreaker is a volunteer open-source project, not a company.
            </p>

            <h2>The software</h2>
            <p>
              Team StormBreaker builds custom Linux kernels and tools for Android devices. Our source code
              is open and released under the GNU General Public License (GPL). You are free to use, study,
              modify and redistribute it under the terms of that license.
            </p>

            <h2>Flashing is at your own risk</h2>
            <p>
              Custom kernels are for advanced users. Installing one usually requires an unlocked bootloader
              and root access, and it can void your warranty, wipe your data, or in rare cases leave a device
              unbootable. You install and use our software <strong>entirely at your own risk</strong>. You are
              responsible for reading instructions, keeping backups, and knowing what you are doing.
            </p>

            <h2>No warranty</h2>
            <p>
              Our software and this website are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
              implied. To the fullest extent permitted by law, Team StormBreaker and its contributors are not
              liable for any damage, data loss, or device malfunction arising from the use of our kernels,
              tools, or this site.
            </p>

            <h2>Downloads and donations</h2>
            <p>
              Downloads are hosted on third-party services such as SourceForge. Donations are handled by
              PayPal. We do not process payments ourselves and never see your payment details. Donations are
              voluntary gifts, not purchases, and are non-refundable. No feature is ever paywalled.
            </p>

            <h2>Trademarks and third parties</h2>
            <p>
              Android, device names, chipset names and Custom ROM projects mentioned on this site are the
              property of their respective owners, and their mention does not imply endorsement. Links to
              third-party sites are provided for convenience; we are not responsible for their content.
            </p>

            <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
            <p>
              Please do not use our project, repositories or community spaces to harass others, distribute
              malware, or break the law. Our community spaces are also governed by our
              <a href="/about/coc/">Code of Conduct</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Changes</h2>
            <p>
              We may update these terms as the project evolves. Continued use of the site means you accept
              the current version.
            </p>

            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <p>
              Questions? Email us at <a href={`mailto:${SOCIAL.email}`}>{SOCIAL.email}</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
